  { number := 208, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 209, text := "" },
  { number := 210, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 211, text := "" },
  { number := 212, text := "1. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read; the specification is also encoded in Lean; proofs live in separate Lean modules; Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URLs; `spec_check` remains form and is not meaning (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 213, text := "2. The crate name is `majestic` and the installed command is `memex` (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 214, text := "3. Uncompressed archives begin with `MAJESTIC` plus byte `0x01`, use extension `.majestic`, and are not Tech Tree `.sstt` files (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 215, text := "4. Archive data lives under `$HOME/memex` except for an explicit single ingest output path; a home scan does not walk that data root as a source (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 216, text := "5. Tech Tree `.sstt` remains specification 0011; `memex` MAY later load a `.sstt` file; this Lake package includes a `.sstt` writer; `btc-verified` is a Form 1 pin at `ref/btc-verified`; the command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 217, text := "6. The crate is treated as a version 0.1 proof of concept still being built and not ready for use; beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are treated as ongoing and not ready for use; a `.sstt` producer is not shipped; fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado remain unspecified; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 218, text := "7. The Unlicense of this specifications repository is not treated as a silent grant over `~/majestic` (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 219, text := "8. Every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean`; proofs of those encodings live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`; the named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 220, text := "" },
  { number := 221, text := "This specification is not itself a finished `memex` product. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
  { number := 222, text := "" },
  { number := 223, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to." },
  { number := 224, text := "" },
  { number := 225, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 226, text := "" },
  { number := 227, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 228, text := "" },
  { number := 229, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 230, text := "" },
  { number := 231, text := "1. fargo is not specified. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, 0011, or 0012 for fargo." },
  { number := 232, text := "2. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is not specified. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 233, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is Formal Vibefication (`0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) (`0009_PDOSS.md`). Unlicense remains the license. Number 0010 is Surmount Systems (`0010_Surmount_Systems.md`). Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). Number 0012 is this specification. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 234, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 235, text := "5. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) by operator order. Unlicense remains the license. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present." },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "### 6.2 Crate still being built" },
  { number := 238, text := "" },
  { number := 239, text := "1. The crate at `~/majestic` is version 0.1. It is still being built. Ingest shapes, search flags, `MCP` tools, `ACP` local functions, HTTP bind, and `zstd` helpers named in that crate README may change. This specification does not freeze that README as a wire." },
  { number := 240, text := "2. Named export shapes in that README (Grok dump JSON, `ChatGPT` conversations JSON, Telegram Desktop JSON, `grok-oss` session `JSONL`, `grok-oss` `sqlite` chats, agent reports, `Obsidian` vault, markdown tree) are crate work in progress. They are not a claim that every service export already ingests without loss." },
  { number := 241, text := "3. Leftover `{account}.archive` files, `memex compress` writing `FILE.majestic.zst`, and `memex decompress` are crate details. They are not a second on disk magic." },
  { number := 242, text := "4. Search uses an embedded `ripgrep` engine in that crate. It does not spawn `rg`. That engine is not the full `rg` CLI." },
  { number := 243, text := "5. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that product is ready for use." },
  { number := 244, text := "6. This specifications repository does not wait on a finished `memex` command. The crate at `~/majestic` remains a version 0.1 proof of concept still being built. This document does not freeze a finished command as a named gate. Companion Lean encodes a mash of waiting on a finished `memex` command as `False`." },
  { number := 245, text := "" },
  { number := 246, text := "### 6.3 Format and product that are not shipped here" },
  { number := 247, text := "" },
  { number := 248, text := "1. Specification 0011 specifies `.sstt`. This format is not `.sstt`. This Lake package includes a Lean writer (`lean/Sstt.lean`). That writer is not a shipped memex product. Magic `MAJESTIC` plus byte `0x01` and extension `.majestic` remain distinct from Tech Tree magic `SSTECHTREE01` and extension `.sstt`. A later load of a `.sstt` file does not mix those formats. Companion Lean encodes a mash of those formats as `False`. This document does not claim that product is finished." },
  { number := 249, text := "2. Bitcoin `CompactSize` as proved in `btc-verified` is prior Lean proof for Tech Tree files. The Form 1 pin is `ref/btc-verified`. This Lake package does not vendor those theorems." },
  { number := 250, text := "3. `repo_links_check` does not parse every HTML `href`. The floor is markdown `[text](target)` links. Reference style links are residual." },
  { number := 251, text := "4. Bush 1945 is unpinned prior art. It is not under `ref/`. This effort does not add a Form 2 pin of that essay. Companion Lean does not encode Bush 1945 as a Clause 12 pin." },
  { number := 252, text := "" },
  { number := 253, text := "### 6.4 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 254, text := "" },
  { number := 255, text := "1. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 256, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md`. This document does not claim that match already holds." },
  { number := 257, text := "3. `lean/MemexSpec.lean` encodes selected claims. `lean/MemexProofs.lean` proves those claims. `0012_Majestic_Memex.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0012.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that the crate is finished. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use." },
  { number := 258, text := "4. Companion Lean encodes clashes this document already states as `False`. A mash of `.majestic` archives with `.sstt` files is `False`. A mash of magic `MAJESTIC` with `SSTECHTREE01` is `False`. A mash of crate name `majestic` with command `memex` is `False`. A mash of this repository Unlicense covering `~/majestic` is `False`. A mash of spec encodings with proofs is `False`. A mash that the crate is ready for use is `False`. A mash that the crate never started is `False`. A mash of waiting on a finished `memex` command is `False`. A mash that a later load of `.sstt` makes a `.majestic` archive a Tech Tree file is `False`. A mash that the Lake `.sstt` writer is a shipped memex product is `False`. A mash that companion Lean proves the crate is finished is `False`. Those encodings are not a finished `memex` command." },
  { number := 259, text := "" },
  { number := 260, text := "### 6.5 Pins and licenses this document does not add" },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "1. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are not pins of this specifications repository's `ref/`. `0002_Systems_Lean.md` places those Form 1 pins in the Systems Lean product tree. This repository MUST NOT copy those four trees into this repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 263, text := "2. `btc-verified` is a Form 1 pin of this repository's `ref/` at `ref/btc-verified`." },
  { number := 264, text := "3. Formal Vibefication essays are cited by URL. They are not Clause 12 pins. This repository does not vendor those essays as Form 2 copies under `ref/`. Full license text is still not published on https://proofofkeags.com . Do not invent that license." },
  { number := 265, text := "4. The Unlicense of this specifications repository does not silently cover `~/majestic`. That crate has its own `UNLICENSE.md`. Citing the crate README does not move that tree into this repository." },
  { number := 266, text := "" },
  { number := 267, text := "### 6.6 Earlier numbered specifications name this document" },
  { number := 268, text := "" },
  { number := 269, text := "Numbered specifications `0005_CATE.md`, `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`, `0009_PDOSS.md`, `0010_Surmount_Systems.md`, and `0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md` name number 0012 as Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and as specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. This 1.0.0 created `0012_Majestic_Memex.md` as a published registry file." },
  { number := 270, text := "" },
