  { number := 279, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260827" },
  { number := 280, text := "" },
  { number := 281, text := "First publication of Majestic `Memex` as numbered specification 0012 with file name `0012_Majestic_Memex.md`. Records that this document is the human contract for crate `majestic`, command `memex`, on disk magic `MAJESTIC` plus byte `0x01`, extension `.majestic`, and data under `$HOME/memex`. Records that this format is not Tech Tree `.sstt` (specification 0011, magic `SSTECHTREE01`). Records that `memex` MAY later load a `.sstt` file. Records that the crate is a version 0.1 proof of concept still being built and is not ready for use. Records Formal Vibefication with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and back linking. Records that the Unlicense of this specifications repository does not silently dedicate `~/majestic`. Requires residual honesty that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are ongoing and not ready for use." },
  { number := 282, text := "" },
  { number := 283, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; Continuous Integration is specification 0007; Formal Vibefication is specification 0008; Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) is specification 0009; Unlicense remains the license; the word catalog is owned by CATE as specification 0005; a numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist; Surmount Systems is specification 0010; Surmount Systems Tech Tree is specification 0011; this specification is number 0012; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP is not specified; Carbonado has no assigned number; Lean Machine is specified as `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown, with proofs in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, checked by `line_encodings_check`; this document does not claim that a finished `memex` product exists." },
